A||N||65||grinthock||PA Tech Day - I'm Home !||||10||
Z||000000||grinthock||10-07-2001||07:39 PM||||Well everyone I made it home.  It was 625 Kilometers each way or 387 Miles.  <P>The Pa landscapes were SPECTACULAR both while I was attending and the drive back (drive on the way there was nightime in DENSE FOG!)<P>The drive down was interesting, almost nailed 2 deer and a porcupine, managed to get a ticket for 76 in a 65 in NY state.<P>For anyone who has NOT enjoyed the hospitality or friendliness of the PA crowd, what the heck are you waiting for?!?  This group is the #1 fiero club I have ever been to.  They are cheerful, fun, and MORE helpful than you can imagine, many a club could learn from this team!<P>Many thanks goto Dave (skitime) and Jen (FieroChic) and her dad Jim for bording me for 2 days while I was down.  I really appriciate it, (eh?), <P>While I was down I had a chance to see the R134 conversion a GREAT demo by Jim!  Meet the whole PA team, see SkiTime's AMAZING ride in person, see the Gilbert Fieroworld which is amazing, AND got to PARTY with the 2 BEST fiero women on the planet (let me rub the stuff off my nose, gimmie a sec!).  We went out to see a movie, cruised around town and had a BLAST.  PICS are on the way everyone, I just got in so check this thread tonight!<P>There are some AMAZING pics that will be posted, so check back it will be worth it. <P>The Gilbert family is a true american fiero legend, they deserve our gratitude for their alligance to the fiero community giving up their home, countless prep hrs and their time to run both the Tech day and Road Ralley.<P>I would like to thank Rodney Dickman and the other sponsors for sponsoring this event, they made it possible to have door prizes.  RODNEY THANKS!! I won your FIERO 3RD brake OVERLAY!! Installed it within an HOUR, and it looked GREAT (after replacing my bulb which had burtn out!  Thanks Jim for letting me grab one from the Gilbert Bone Yard)<P><BR>I would like to thank Hagster (Don) for being my navigator in the Road Rally and bringing us a 3rd place (We were robbed dude, I know, but hey who cares!)<P>I gotta thank the PA crowd and Jen for the certificate for "Longest Distance Traveled to Attend"<P>I had a great time meeting EVERYONE who's name's I hardly remember, I apoligize but you are all such a great crew.<P>I hope some day we can host event like this up in Canada.  I also hope that you will run another event soon to give me an excuse to come back down there.  It may sound strange (weak guy moment!) but leaving you all today put a tear to my eye.  You treated me like family and most of all treated me like friends. <P>Well that's all the talk till the pics are posted, I will post small pics here for you modem guys then a full size album will be available on FieroWorld later (private URL to be posted here)<P>I guess I can't have anymore to say!  <BR>Thanks again!<p>[This message has been edited by grinthock (edited 10-07-2001).]||||reg||10
Z||000001||Fierochic88||10-07-2001||07:57 PM||||Hey Grinthock or Justin  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>Thanks for coming and glad you enjoyed your trip!  You definitely have to come again and we'll even let you bring Heather  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">  Can't wait to see the pics!<P>Also, thanks to Denny for the beautiful certificate, Eh?!!!!<P><BR>Jennifer (coming soon : new sig pic!)<P>------------------<BR>IM Username:  FieroChic88<BR>Silver 1988 GT<BR>Silver 1986 2m4<BR>Cobalt Blue 85 GT<P>     <IMG SRC="http://www.webjolt.f2s.com/pictures/jenscar-sig1.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000002||FieroLisa||10-07-2001||08:04 PM||||Justin: 2 words: Jew Power!!!!!  (for people who have something against me saying that, hush cause we're both Jewish and its just an inside joke  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> )<P>Oh and I did not lose it!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>Good meeting you, I'm sure I'll see ya later- bye!||||reg||1
