Z||000017||Denny||10-08-2001||07:44 AM||||Great pictures, Justin!<P>Thanks for coming, and we're all glad you had such a great time! We try . . .<P>Hope to see you again, perhaps at Carlisle next spring?<P>BTW, I married a Jew, so I know they ain't all bad!    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>Oh yeah! Almost forgot! Hey Jen, did you (or your pappy) notice I left my "signature" on your driveway? Look at hill, just as you start up from the parking area . . . just my contribution to the asphalt . . . <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><p>[This message has been edited by Denny (edited 10-08-2001).]||||reg||14
Z||000018||grinthock||10-08-2001||07:57 AM||||72vinman -- Well if you drive NON stop and don't even stop for GAS then it's like 6 hrs.  in all honesty it's 7.5.  It's about 650 Klms.  Keep in mind you can't speed like you can in Canada.  I got a Radar detector while I was there at a 2nd hand hock shop I drove past ($25 USD) it saved my rear twice on the way back, twice from KA cops and once from a laser bandit.<P>TooManyFieros - To be totally honest?  I am not sure, they were just sort of sitting on the side of the road and asked me to take pics of them!  I have NEVER seen them before! The blond tho says she gets all her good looks from her parents and especially Dad.<P>Carlisle Srping show - I AM IN!  I can't wait to come back!  I woke up this morning alone, nobody is here, even BanditBalz has gone away for the weekend! <P>(Here is a secret FieroLisa fact -- she's a wreck in the morning!)<P>||||reg||1
